          "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "Dynamically scheduling paired opposite starting columns should reduce data-dependent imbalance relative to contiguous band partitions. Each full task contains n+1 bands, amortizing scheduling overhead while keeping each band's counting entirely thread-local.",
          "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
            "files": [
              "src/main.cpp"
            ],
            "retained": [
              "Pair starting columns j and n+1-j, processing the central column only once.",
              "Dynamically distribute coarse paired tasks across at most four workers, with no synchronization inside band counting.",
              "Give each worker a reusable private frequency map and a 64-bit subtotal, combining results only after completion.",
              "Select serial, two-worker or four-worker execution from estimated row visits and available task count.",
              "Reset prefix-column zero explicitly on every solve call while preserving the counting kernel and input/output behavior."
            ]
          },
          "status": "valid",
